A||N||3||reddog||Fuel pressure Question||||1||
Z||000000||reddog||11-23-2001||09:26 PM||||Ok I just put the Fiero Stores fuel pressure guage on my 86 GT 2.8! My question is what should the pressure be at idle? Mine reads just below 40psi at idle and drops about 8psi when throttled up to about 2500rpm is this normal?I also noticed that once the gauge was installed the idle rpms dropped about 150-200 rpms is this common when istalling the guage with an s shape adapter like the Fiero stores guage set-up?<P>------------------<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Picturenew_sig.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000001||Formula88||11-23-2001||10:54 PM||||If I remember the spec on my 88 2.8, it's 45psi with the key 'on' but the engine off.  Should be above 40psi with the engine running.  Check your fuel filter - easy to change and only about $6.  Just in front of the right rear tire.  ||||reg||1
Z||000002||reddog||11-23-2001||11:05 PM||||I just changed the fuel filter about 3 weeks ago. don't think I put it on backward!Could it even run with it on backwards? What would cause it to have lower fuel pressure?<P>------------------<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Picturenew_sig.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000003||camon||11-23-2001||11:28 PM||||Not sure about the low fuel pressure!<P>But if the filter is on backwards I don't believe it would work correctly.<P>Just look under car and see if it is on right.....mine (dechutes) has an arrow to show flow direction (yours may too).<P>------------------<BR>Keith||||reg||1
